 "notes": "CASPEr-Gradient Low-Field commissioning search. Curve traced from Fig. 3 (figures/ALPlimits.png in the e-print, raster) 'Main scan' (green) curve, the deepest of the three sequential scans and the one matching the quoted headline constraint |g_ap| <= 3e-2 GeV^-1 (95% CL) over 5.576741-5.577733 neV (240 Hz window at 1.348570 MHz). Axis calibration from tick marks (log-y ticks 3-9 x10^-2 GeV^-1, residuals <0.05%); x converted via m = h*nu with nu = 1348450 Hz + offset; endpoints reproduce the stated mass range. Paper's native coupling is g_ap in GeV^-1 defined via H = g_ap grad(a).I (Eq. 2); converted to the canonical dimensionless g_ap with the task 2m_N rule: g_ap = 2*m_p*g[GeV^-1] (extracted GeV^-1 values ranged 3.31e-2 down to 2.86e-2). Caveat: the paper writes the Hamiltonian with nuclear spin I rather than sigma=2I; if taken literally the conversion would be m_p*g (factor 2 lower). Sampled at the ~40 scan-step markers (6 Hz spacing).",
